+    selection of every block, in order, on the side stream (after the current stream's work so far, and after the row
+    split's side stream, so no two streams run collectives at once), the sparse attention of block j on the current
+    stream once block j's selection is done. The current stream ends after every selection (it waits on the last
+    block's event), so nothing after this call sees the side stream running, and the scratch below, allocated on the
+    current stream before the side stream uses it, is freed only after it is done with."""
+
